{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 120, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op on the final edge into the output node with a 3x3 conv adds useful capacity, more so than replacing none or skip (e.g. exp 9)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 1 is already conv-processed, a conv on edge 1->3 is largely redundant; gains are big only when edge 0 is none/skip/pool (exps 32-34 vs 31, 35-39)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for avg pooling removes learnable capacity on the edge between the intermediate nodes (exps 41, 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing skip with pooling costs little or even helps, whereas replacing a conv costs a lot (exps 42, 50 vs 41)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a pooling edge into node 2 to a conv adds capacity, whereas replacing skip/none often disrupts gradient flow (exp 54 vs 51, 53)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a conv on the edge from node 2 to the output loses capacity, whereas deleting pool or skip is neutral or helpful (exps 71, 79 vs 74, 75)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a conv on the first edge removes a learnable path, more harmful than removing skip/pool/1x1 (domain prior; exps 22 vs 25-28)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv on edge 1->3 with an identity loses capacity, while replacing none/1x1/pool is neutral or positive (exps 91, 95, 98 vs 92-94, 96)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling into the output with a skip yields a clean residual path and large gains (exp 93)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a harmful pooling edge into the output helps far more than removing a conv (exp 75 vs 71, 79)."}], "tok": 18029, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3